5,1,1,talk,Toshio,,"Since our current habit isn't working, we need a sustainable system for the year. I believe we should first clarify the actual costs and the time required to keep the place clean.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. We can't build a fair system without objective data. I'm particularly concerned about the actual time commitment involved in these tasks; we need to know exactly how many hours we're spending.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I concur. However, time and cost are only part of the equation. To be truly equitable, we should also examine the correlation between how much we actually use the spaces and the work we contribute.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,May,,Exactly! But let's not forget the most important part: the quality. It's a gamble every time I walk into the bathroom. We need a standard so we aren't just guessing if a room is actually clean.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with everyone. While the data is important, I really hope we find a system that keeps us all happy and friendly. Let's make sure we choose something that prevents any future misunderstandings or tension.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"To ensure transparency, I'll look into the management office rate sheet and billing, as well as the bathroom spray stock and the tin's receipts. We need to see where the money is actually going.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,I'll take the stopwatch timing of a full pass and the standard terms of the outside firm. I want to compare the actual labor hours against the cost of professional help.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,I shall investigate a fortnight's watch on kitchen use and the absences on the wall calendar. It would be most illuminating to see who is actually present to create the mess we are discussing.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,May,,"I'll check what each housemate counts as done and the bathroom grout after the July scrub. If we can't agree on what ""clean"" actually looks like, no amount of timing or billing will help us.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Midori,,I'll look into the rows recorded in the house chat and the note left by the previous tenants. I want to see where we've struggled before so we can avoid the same arguments this year.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"That covers the essential data points. Once we have these facts, we can determine if a self-managed rotation or a paid service is more viable for our budget and schedules.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"It is a logical approach. By comparing the time we spend manually cleaning with the cost of a professional service, we can determine if the trade-off is worth the financial expense.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. While the financial trade-off is a compelling metric, I suspect we may find that the perceived burden is not distributed as evenly as our current assumptions suggest. Data will be our best mediator.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,May,,"I just hope we stop playing ""cleaning roulette."" If the data shows we're all imagining different versions of ""clean,"" we'll have to get very specific about the rules this time. No more guessing!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree. Being specific might seem strict, but it's actually kinder in the long run. If we're all on the same page, we can avoid those little frustrations that build up and hurt our friendships.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Toshio,,Let's proceed then. We have our assignments. I expect we can all be thorough in our research so that we can make a decision based on facts rather than feelings in the next round.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will ensure my timing is precise. Having a clear baseline of the actual hours required is the only way to determine if our current arrangement is truly sustainable or simply an invisible drain on our time.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall apply the same rigor to my observations. It would be a pity to design a sophisticated system only to discover it is based on the fiction that we all occupy these rooms with equal frequency.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,May,,"I'm on it! I'll get to the bottom of these ""standards"" of ours. I can't wait to see if we're all actually talking about the same thing when we say a room is clean. See you all soon!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Midori,,I'll do my best to find some helpful insights. I'm looking forward to seeing what we all discover so we can find a peaceful solution that works for everyone. See you all in the next round!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
