60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the most logical. It provides the professional standard May wants and eliminates the labor drain Ryuji noted. Most importantly, a monthly invoice allows for a transparent, centralized billing process to end the out-of-pocket confusion.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. Option B is the only choice that meaningfully addresses the time expenditure. Spending over 100 minutes per pass is an unsustainable drain on our productivity and mental energy that a professional service effectively removes.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"While Option B is efficient, it still leaves the question of cost distribution open. However, compared to the rigid unfairness of a rota or the chaos of standing assignments, it is the most rational foundation for a fair agreement.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Option B is the only one that actually solves my problem! A professional service means a professional result. No more guessing, no more ""cleaning roulette,"" and no more staring at black grout. I'm all in!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm leaning toward Option B too. While it costs money, it removes the need for us to remind or nag each other about chores, which is where our past arguments started. It seems like the safest way to keep us all friends.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, we can simply agree to a flat monthly fee for the service and a shared fund for supplies. This removes the ambiguity of who paid for what and ensures no one is left out of pocket.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, a flat fee is acceptable. While it doesn't perfectly solve the usage disparity Benjamin mentioned, the time saved is a universal benefit. The cost is a fair trade for reclaiming those hours of labor every month.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, @Ryuji, a flat fee is a pragmatic compromise. While it lacks mathematical precision regarding usage, it is far more elegant than the interpersonal friction a rota would inevitably generate. I can accept this for the sake of harmony.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,See? We're finally agreeing! Let's stop over-analyzing the math and just commit to the professional service. I'm tired of the unpredictability; I just want to walk into a clean room without holding my breath.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,I'm so glad we're all on the same page. Option B feels like the kindest choice because it takes the pressure off us and lets us focus on being housemates instead of managers. I'm happy to vote for it!,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Since we have reached a consensus on the benefits of Option B, I see no reason to delay. It solves the financial ambiguity and the labor issue simultaneously. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I am also ready. The data on time expenditure makes the choice clear; the cost of the service is a reasonable price to pay for the recovery of our time and peace of mind.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall join the consensus. While I still find the usage disparity a curious oversight, the avoidance of a rigid rota is a victory for logic and peace. I am ready to vote for Option B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"Finally! I'm so relieved we're doing this. No more guessing, no more grout nightmares, and no more stress. I'm voting for Option B in a heartbeat!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm really happy we've found a solution that everyone likes. It feels like a weight has been lifted, and I'm sure this will keep our home peaceful. I'm ready to vote for Option B too!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"It is settled. Option B provides the financial transparency and professional consistency we require. I will vote for the Paid Cleaning Service to ensure we have a clear, centralized system for the coming year.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will also vote for Option B. Eliminating the significant time drain of manual cleaning is the most rational decision for our long-term productivity and well-being. It is the only sustainable path forward.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall cast my vote for Option B. While a usage-based fee would be the pinnacle of fairness, a professional service is a far more sophisticated solution than any rota we could devise. Logic dictates we prioritize peace.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting for Option B! I can't wait to finally stop playing cleaning roulette and actually enjoy our shared spaces. Let's get this professional service started and put the grout nightmares behind us!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'm voting for Option B as well. I'm so relieved we've found a way to keep the house clean without risking our friendships. Let's make this year a happy and peaceful one for all of us!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
